<title>MEXICO: Mexicana to update series A shares.</title>
<headline>Mexicana to update series A shares.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Airline Corporacion Mexicana de Aviacion S.A. de C.V. (CMA) said in a report to the Mexican stock market that it would update on Thursday the number of its series A shares, as agreed at a special shareholders' meeting held on March 4, 1996.</p>
<p>CMA said in its report that the new number of series A shares after the updating would be 5,898,097,378.</p>
<p>The increase in shares was part of the company's financial and corporate restructuring program. CMA has since been consolidated into the holding company Cintra.</p>
<p>-- Karina Balderas, Mexico City newsroom, +525 728-9562</p>
